# Rust
# Unanchored so it matches at ANY depth. The previous root-anchored `/target/`
# missed faucet/target/, which is how 1,115 build-artifact files (fingerprint
# stamps, .rustc_info.json, a stale .cargo-lock) ended up tracked in git.
# INTEGRATOR: `git rm -r --cached faucet/target` is still required - this
# pattern stops new artifacts, it does not untrack existing ones.
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored.
# This workspace ships binaries (arc-node) to third-party operators, and
# binary-producing workspaces commit their lockfile; only libraries omit it.
# Without a tracked lock, no build is reproducible from its tag, `--locked`
# cannot be used in CI, cargo-deny/advisory scanning has nothing stable to
# walk, and Dependabot has no lock to bump.
# INTEGRATOR: the lockfile is currently untracked, so it needs an explicit
# `git add -f Cargo.lock` once (the -f is only needed if a stale ignore entry
# is still cached).

# Node / Explorer
# Unanchored: desktop/, sdk/typescript/ and sdks/typescript/ all have npm
# projects and were previously unignored, escaping tracking only because
# nobody had run npm install there.
**/node_modules/
explorer/node_modules/
explorer/.next/
explorer/dist/
explorer/.env.local

# SDK
sdk/node_modules/
sdk/dist/

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Benchmark export
explorer/public/benchmark-data/

# Deploy state
deploy/.node-ips
rustc-ice*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code local config (per-machine, not for git)
.claude/
